A||||14||Tom88gt||4x10 speakers?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||01-12-2000||10:04 AM||||Any recommendations for 4x10 speakers?<P>Pioneer and Kenwood offer 4x10s but they are cheap (paper drivers, cone tweeters, foam surrounds) and cost $99!!!<P>I can mount a plate, 4x6, 4", etc but I'd rather use a 4x10 with a polymer/treated driver, dome tweeters and rubber surrounds.  <P>Has anyone found other brand/model speakers besides the cheap Radio Shack/Pep Boys stock replacements.  I know may find these speakers work just fine but I've become addicted to Polks, Pyle Drivers, JBLs, etc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||01-11-2000||04:25 PM||||The Pioneer TS-A4105 4" X 10" speakers have polymer drivers and dome tweeters. If you can still find the Kicker Impulse speakers, they are excellent with all the right features.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||01-11-2000||04:39 PM||||Bat, are the Pioneers 2 or 3 way?  I'll look for them.  Do you know of any good web sites besides Crutchfield (good but few 4x10s)?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-11-2000||05:45 PM||||I'm on the Cerwin-Vega mailing list and I just got an email from them last week saying something about new car speaker coming out soon.  I used to have a set of their speakers in the house (stolen <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) and they were awsome!  Hopefully C-V will have some 4x10 for our Fieros.  I'll post something when I find out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||01-11-2000||07:51 PM||||The Pioneer TS-A4105 is a 3 way speaker. The Pioneer TS-A4103 4" X 10" is cheaper and does have the poly drivers, but it's only a 2 way with a cone tweeter. I don't know of any good car audio websites. I'm always nosing around in the Crutchfield catalog and the Best Buy store. Getting ready to buy a new home theater receiver and another pair of speakers (probably Yamaha for both), so I've been in the audio section quite often lately.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave85||01-11-2000||09:25 PM||||For car audio you can try <A HREF="http://www.autotoys.com" TARGET=_blank>www.autotoys.com</A>  They have about the best prices I've found. Of the 4x10's I've heard(Pioneer,Alpine,Kenwood) the Pioneers are the best sounding with the best frequency response.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||01-11-2000||11:53 PM||||I have the 2-way pioneer's in my dash, and they are way better than the stock speakers.  I paid around $80 for them at Wally World 6 years ago, and I'm driving them directly from a Panasonic 22Wattx4 CD player.  The 4x6 version doesn't sound any better than stock, to me, but mine came from a junkyard for $5, so they may be trashed anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000007||grizco||01-12-2000||01:16 AM||||You can also fit 5 1/4" speakers in the 4X10 opening on the fiero with a little trimming on the area of the dash under the factory grilles. I currently have a 5 1/4" Kenwood 2 way and a 4" Profile 2 way in the dash of my car,powered by a 500 watt Jenson Amp. (still haven't turned the volume all the way up, half volume is plenty loud enough). With the grilles on the car looks completely stock and going with 5 1/4" speakers gives you alot more selection.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||01-12-2000||08:53 AM||||I picked up my 4x10 3-ways at Wal-Mart as well.  You never can tell what youll find in there sometimes.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ggarsk||01-12-2000||10:24 AM||||Check out Crutchfield's. I believe they have 4x10 Polks. I just got a pair of 4x6 Infinity 2 ways to put in my dash. I'm going to make a plate to bolt in place of the 4x10's and mount the 4x6's on it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||01-12-2000||04:46 PM||||Do a search for Dynaudio speakers on the web. They make hundreds of great speakers cheap.I think they make speakers for high buck home audio systems.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tom88gt||01-12-2000||05:16 PM||||I did a "car speaker" & "car stereo" web search.  I found a lot of sources for 4x10s.  Most were off-brands or unknown brands.  I found several 4x10s under the $50 mark but they mostly had foam surrounds and cone tweeters.  <P>One pair did look interesting.  Poly driver, byutl rubber surround, dome tweeters.  "AudioBhan"??? only $46 pr and some matching 4x6s for same/less?  However, I've never heard of this company.  The tweeter bracket is this large "hip" looking plastic piece that covers most of the driver and I think it would block the sound and cause destructive interferrence.<P>I did find some awsome JBL GTO series 4x10s for $79 and 4x6 for $69 + shipping at "Buy It Now".  I got a great deal on a JBL home system from them a while back.  I've heard plenty of JBL GTOs (5.25, 6.5, 4x6) and have no problem buying 4x10s "un-heard" so to speak.  <P>Well, I pulled the covers off the dash and found some old Alpines (paper drivers and cone tweeters) that are in good shape.  So I'll take some time to think about dropping $150 on the JBL GTOs.  But, if anyone needs speakers now, I highly recommend the JBLs.  I'll be doing it, sooner or later.<P>Thanks for everyone's responses.||||reg||1
Z||000012||HF6582||01-12-2000||08:37 PM||||I have the Kicker impulse 4x10 in my 86gt and they sound really good. I found them at a audio store and they were a little expensive but worth the money.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||01-14-2000||12:11 PM||||I have 2 pairs of Eclipse 4" coaxial and they respond much better than the Pioneer 4x10s i got from circuit city. made a plate from 1/4 fiberboard and they seem to fill the void very sweetly! Very clear! Driven by a Kenwood KAC-626... going for clarity, go with a round speaker!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tom88gt||01-14-2000||02:53 PM||||I've wondered about that myself.  Why would a non-round speaker be less accurate?  <P>I can only guess that the "long" sides would have less rigidity and distort more easily.  <P>But, the speaker edges are supported all around.  <P>Also, 4x10s are more midrange, and when crossed over, will not be handling low frequencies, which require the speaker to have a long excursion.  <P>But higher frequencies have way more cycles per second, even though the speaker bearly moves at these frequencies.<P>I guess eveything is a compromise.  Buy what sounds best to you.  Just don't be fooled by volume (the loudest in the demo room always "sounds" better)||||reg||1
